  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 92b2c8003586277498a007ee213cc22b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Log - Fractals
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FloppyData
  diskName: Log - Fractals
  logTitle: Structural Noise Report
  author: Capt. Thomas Eriksen
  shipName: 027-Lifthrasir
  dateRecorded: '[Mission timestamp TBD]'
  logText: "I've been hearing an intermittent creaking noise from somewhere along
    the starboard side of the ship.\r\nInitially I attributed it to thermal expansion,
    but the frequency has increased over the past several hours. The sound is inconsistent
    with the normal stresses I've observed during previous flight operations.\r\nThere
    are no corresponding pressure fluctuations or structural warnings.\r\nI've inspected
    the accessible sections of the hull and found nothing out of place.\r\nI'll continue
    monitoring it. There's no indication of an immediate hazard.\n\r\n[ENTRY APPENDED
    \u2014 TIME TBD]\r\nSomething is wrong with the corridor outside the habitation
    compartment.\r\nI noticed it while returning from the equipment bay. I could
    see the doorway at the far end, but it appeared much farther away than it should
    have been.\r\nI thought it was a trick of the lighting.\r\nI walked toward it.
    After several steps, I stopped. The distance hadn't changed.\r\nI returned to
    the habitation compartment and checked the internal layout. Nothing has been
    modified.\r\nI can hear the creaking again.\r\nI'm going to take another look.\r\n"
